{
  "id": 102930785,
  "iid": 3254,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Remove unnecessary null check in diameter dissector",
  "description": "`dissect_diameter_mip6_feature_vector` is checking whether the `data` argument\n(assigned to `diam_sub_dis_inf`) is null, but later dereferences it outside\nthe conditional, so if it was null it would crash anyway. It doesn't seem\npossible for the `data` argument to actually be null, so this commit removes\nthe redundant check. I'm also adding an assert to document the non-null\nassumption.\n\nBug found by clang static analyzer.\n\nFixes #17427.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-06-05T23:59:52.784Z",
  "updated_at": "2021-06-09T14:13:19.412Z",
